From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 05:29:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] scratch GC: preserve unreadable nested Git repos as
 complete filesystem bytes

Problem: worker-2 retained seven terminal scratch trees (~2 GB) across repeated
hourly passes because Git inspection failed before complete payload creation.

Five whys (happened):
1. Trees survive retention because archive_workspace raises ArchiveRefused.
2. Git cannot inspect malformed/unsupported MIDX, missing blobs, broken repo
   metadata or vanished alternate object paths (the latter is not ref normalization).
3. archive_repo is mandatory and precedes _write_payload; omission planning can
   decline optimization, but subsequent Git inspection aborts the whole archive.
4. Optional Git summaries were treated as a prerequisite to preserving bytes,
   despite the independently verified complete filesystem payload.
5. Coverage encoded malformed repo shapes as permanent refusals instead of
   checking that existing source bytes remain recoverable without Git.

Root (not caught): keep reasons formerly stayed in rotating core logs; the
scheduled wrapper returned success for completed sweeps and healthy free space,
not zero retained trees. #3114/#3117 exposed the backlog, but changed reporting
only. Existing partial-clone and shape fixes did not cover interpretation errors.
Recurrence: follows 2567ea4e31 / 707cac9f6e; those repaired specific shapes, not
this pre-payload prerequisite. The symlinked-home fix is independent.

Countermeasure: distinguish read-only Git inspection failures from archive
write/verification failures. Discard ALL optional output and omission plans on
inspection failure, then preserve the entire workspace through the existing
verified, fsynced, mutation-fenced filesystem payload. Record git-fallback.json.
No source tree is deleted by fallback; existing GC custody/ownership/detach
fences still authorize removal. Existing missing objects are not repaired.
External gitdirs remain fail-closed (external_gitdir); unsafe discovery, payload,
fsync, and bundle verification failures still refuse. Disabled scratch retention
already logs reason=retention_disabled. Worker no-archive policy applies to its
separate linked-worktree sweep, not this Kanban scratch path.

worker-workspace-gc.last.json ok remains correctly defined as successful sweep
execution plus >=25 GiB free capacity, not reclamation completeness. Detailed
keeps are now relayed; no state change required.

Proof:
- Base 5ae5b5e9e5: 9/9 new regressions RED, five injected rc128 classes and four
  real malformed-MIDX/missing-blob/broken-repo/vanished-alternate fixtures.
- 12 archive consumer test files: 352 passed; focused final suite: 18 passed.
- Payload/verify/fsync/detach failures, external gitdir, disabled retention and
  partial-output/omission disposal covered. Every source file compared bytewise.
- Removing external-gitdir guard: 1 failure; broadening classification to archive
  writes/verification: 2 failures. Mutants restored; final suite green.
- scripts/check --base origin/main: 20 checks passed.

Live acceptance remains on t_08eee0f380afe546: merged revision installed on worker-2
and a natural scheduled GC pass after refusal backoff, never a card-shell GC.
